Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 2.1.0
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Integrates paired single-cell RNA and ATAC regulatory evidence
    with genome-scale metabolic reaction analysis. When two or more condition
    levels are available, RegCompass fits one comparable condition-aware Pando
    design per broad cell type and uses outer-heldout TF-by-ATAC projections.
    When condition metadata are absent or contain one level, it automatically
    runs the original Pando infer_grn workflow and enters its standard
    coefficients into the same reaction-support and penalty path without
    calculating condition coefficients. SuperCell receives broad cell type and
    condition as separate native cell.annotation and cell.split.condition
    inputs; no concatenated condition-by-cell-type metadata field is created.
    Metacell RNA and ATAC counts are aggregated from exact SuperCell membership.
    RNA latent-expression priors are estimated by broad cell type, regulatory
    modifiers act on bounded RNA-support odds, GPR rules produce reaction
    expression, and missing reaction expression receives the COMPASS maximum
    expression-linked penalty. Each medium uses one shared union GEM and global
    FASTCORE completion. Canonical behavior is implemented directly in the
    defining functions; runtime function replacement and schema rewriting are
    not used.
